WEBVTT

open
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Most agent programs run start to finish. When one acts wrongly, you find out after.

title
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.600
ALGAL. Write agent programs that wait, resume, and replay.

step-1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.000
Start. The demo program stops before it acts, with status waiting.

step-2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.400
Decide. The report page names the one action. You approve or deny it.

step-3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.800
Crash. Killed twice on purpose. Finished steps are reused, and an uncertain write is not resent.

step-4
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.700
Verify. Export the run to one file and check its history offline.

proof
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.200
0 writes after you deny. 1 delivery of a finished step, crash or not. 1 send of an interrupted write, never repeated

limits
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.200
What it does not do yet. Packages are unsigned. Your own app still decides which tools a program may use.

end
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.700
ALGAL. algal.computer. Preview. Free and open source.
